ition, may be required for patients unable to meet their caloric needs through oral intake alone. The healthcare system aims to identify, prevent, and treat this condition to improve patient outcomes and quality of life.\",74\r\n2336,CICLOSPORINA,\"Ciclosporina is an immunosuppressive medication that is primarily used in the treatment of complications following organ transplants. It has been tested for its efficacy in treating alcoholic liver disease (ALD) but has not shown significant clinical benefits. The drug can lead to various side effects, including diarrhea and neurological issues, which may improve upon discontinuation of the medication. Additionally, ciclosporina can contribute to the development of hypomagnesemia in patients undergoing chemotherapy and may cause alterations in lipid metabolism. It is important to note that the levels of ciclosporina in the body can be increased by the consumption of grapefruit juice, and the medication may also interact with weight loss drugs.\",6\r\n3047,PACIENTES ONCOLÓGICOS,\"PACIENTES ONCOLÓGICOS refers to individuals diagnosed with cancer who may require tailored dietary plans and specialized nutritional support during their treatment. This group of patients is particularly vulnerable to malnutrition, with prevalence rates that can reach up to 50%. The need for nutritional interventions is critical as these patients often face challenges that can impact their health and quality of life. Additionally, the evaluation of fragility in oncological patients can be beneficial for predicting treatment outcomes. Overall, PACIENTES ONCOLÓGICOS represent a specific population that necessitates careful nutritional assessment and support to enhance their overall well-being during the course of their illness.\",12\r\n2335,CICLOFOSFAMIDA,\"Ciclofosfamida is a medication that serves multiple purposes in medical treatment. It is primarily recognized as an immunosuppressive drug, which is utilized in clinical trials to address inflammatory responses in brain lesions of patients with Adrenoleukodystrophy (ALD). Additionally, ciclofosfamida is commonly used in oncological treatments. However, it is important for patients to take this medication with meals to minimize gastrointestinal discomfort. It is also noteworthy that ciclofosfamida can lead to malabsorption and malnutrition in patients, highlighting the need for careful monitoring during its use.\",2\r\n13313,DESCENSO MASA MAGRA,\"Descenso masa magra refers to the loss of lean body mass, which is a common issue in patients with dysphagia and malnutrition.\",2\r\n610,PÉRDIDA DE MASA MUSCULAR,\"PÉRDIDA DE MASA MUSCULAR, or loss of muscle mass, is a significant indicator of severe malnutrition and is assessed during the global subjective evaluation. This condition can arise from malnutrition and is frequently worsened by dysphagia, particularly in patients suffering from neurological diseases.\",2\r\n13242,INMUNODEPRESIÓN,\"INMUNODEPRESIÓN refers to a medical condition characterized by a weakened immune system, which can result from various factors, including malnutrition and cancer treatments. This state of immunodepression leads to a less effective immune response, making individuals more susceptible to infections and other health complications. Specifically, in the context of cancer patients, malnutrition and dysphagia (difficulty swallowing) are significant contributors to this condition, further exacerbating the challenges faced by those affected.\",2\r\n13312,ALTERACIONES CICATRIZACIÓN,Alteraciones cicatrización are complications in wound healing that can arise from poor nutritional status in cancer patients.,1\r\n3230,COSTES POR PROCESO,\"The costs associated with medical processes, which can increase due to malnutrition during hospitalization\",1\r\n1695,DESNUTRICIÓN LEVE,A classification of malnutrition characterized by a Body Mass Index (BMI) between 17 and 18.4.,1\r\n1697,DESNUTRICIÓN GRAVE,A classification of malnutrition characterized by a Body Mass Index (BMI) less than 16.,1\r\n4968,SÍNDROME DE WERNICKE-KORSAKOFF,\"Wernicke-Korsakoff syndrome is a neurological disorder caused by thiamine deficiency, often associated with chronic alcoholism and malnutrition, leading to confusion and memory issues.\",1\r\n2516,ENFERMEDAD ONCOLÓGICA,\"The entity \"\"ENFERMEDAD ONCOLÓGICA\"\" refers to a type of cancer that can significantly impact the nutritional status of patients, particularly pediatric patients undergoing treatment. This condition may necessitate specialized nutritional support, including enteral nutrition, to address the nutritional needs of these young patients. Additionally, \"\"ENFERMEDAD ONCOLÓGICA\"\" is associated with an increased prevalence of malnutrition, especially in advanced stages of the disease. This highlights the critical importance of nutritional management in the care of individuals affected by cancer.\",1\r\n8012,GRUPOS POBLACIONALES SUSCEPTIBLES,\"Los grupos poblacionales susceptibles incluyen ancianos, pacientes oncológicos y hospitalizados, quienes tienen un mayor riesgo de desnutrición.\",1\r\n13243,MALA CICATRIZACIÓN,\"Poor healing is a condition that can occur due to malnutrition, which may be linked to dysphagia in patients.\",1\r\n13637,AGENTES FARMACOLÓGICOS,Los agentes farmacológicos son tratamientos utilizados en pacientes malnutridos para estimular el apetito y mejorar la función intestinal.,1\r\n13638,PROFESIONAL NUTRICIONAL,El profesional nutricional es un experto que proporciona asesoramiento nutricional a los pacientes para mejorar sus hábitos alimentarios.,1\r\n13315,DESCENSO DEL ESTATUS FUNCIONAL,\"Descenso del estatus funcional refers to the decline in a patient's ability to perform daily activities, often linked to malnutrition.\",1\r\n13314,INCREMENTO DE INFECCIONES,Incremento de infecciones indicates the increased risk of infections due to malnutrition and immunodeficiency in cancer patients.,1\r\n\n\n-----Relationships-----\nhuman_readable_id,sourc